# Line endings are LF everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, a clone on Windows with the common `core.autocrlf=true` gets
# CRLF in every file, and `pnpm format:check` then fails on every file - while
# CI on Linux stays green, because Linux never did the conversion. That split
# is worse than either result on its own: it tells a new contributor the
# repository is broken when it is their checkout that differs.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched, whatever they contain.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.db    binary
*.tgz   binary
